 ## Unreleased — 1.4.0
 
-Nothing yet.
+- `smysl fmt` no longer re-parses its own output when that output is byte-identical to the
+  input. The round-trip check compares the second parse with the first, and for identical text
+  the two are the same parse; already-canonical files (the usual case for `--check` and
+  `--write` as a pre-commit habit) now cost one parse instead of two. Files that change are
+  still verified, and no output differs.
 
